#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:667
#, no-wrap
msgid "Exploiting the `sendmailCmd` option of `git send-email`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:675
msgid ""
"Apart from sending emails via an SMTP server, `git send-email` can also send "
"emails through any application that supports sendmail-like commands. You can "
"read documentation of `--sendmail-cmd=<command>` above for more "
"information.  This ability can be very useful if you want to use another "
"application as an SMTP client for `git send-email`, or if your email "
"provider uses proprietary APIs instead of SMTP to send emails."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:679
msgid ""
"As an example, lets see how to configure https://marlam.de/msmtp/[msmtp], a "
"popular SMTP client found in many Linux distributions. Edit `~/.gitconfig` "
"to instruct `git-send-email` to use it for sending emails."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:683
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[sendemail]\n"
"\tsendmailCmd = /usr/bin/msmtp # Change this to the path where msmtp is installed\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:686
msgid "Links of a few such community maintained helpers are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.adoc:689
msgid ""
"https://marlam.de/msmtp/[msmtp] (popular SMTP client with many features, "
"available for Linux and macOS)"
msgstr ""

